1. Open JavaFX Scene Builder.
2. Create a new JavaFX FXML file.
3. Drag and drop a Label from the Controls section onto the layout.
4. In the Properties panel, set the Label text to Welcome to JavaFX.
5. Drag and drop an ImageView from the Library section onto the layout.
6. In the Properties panel, select an image file for the ImageView.
7. Adjust the size and position of both components.
8. Save the FXML file and preview the GUI.
Expected Output
Welcome to JavaFX









Sample GUI: Label displaying text and ImageView displaying an image.
Result: A JavaFX GUI containing a Label and an ImageView is created successfully using Scene Builder without writing code.
